  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "sp_ecc_proj_add_point_256",
    "file": "wolfssl-sp-math/wolfcrypt/src/sp_c64.c",
    "description": "The crash is caused by calling the low-level SP ECC add routine with overlapping input/output point storage: `sp_ecc_proj_add_point_256` invokes `sp_256_proj_point_add_5(p, p, q, tmp)` (same `p` used as both destination and first source). `sp_256_proj_point_add_5` does not safely support this aliasing pattern and performs reads from corrupted/intermediate state, leading to a wild read/SEGV.",
    "conditions": "From the cryptofuzz harness, `OpECC_Point_Add` calls `ecc_projective_add_point` in the non-safe path (`safe == false`). With SP math enabled and 256-bit modulus, this dispatches into `sp_ecc_proj_add_point_256`, which always uses in-place aliasing (`r == p`). A crafted input that reaches this path (as in the provided PoV) triggers invalid memory access inside `sp_256_proj_point_add_5` during projective point addition."
  },
